<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine economy minister pospones Europe trip.</title>
<headline>Argentine economy minister pospones Europe trip.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine Economy Minister Roque Fernandez has postponed his trip to Europe next week said the ministry Friday, according to state news agency Telam.</p>
<p>Fernandez will still go to Washington next Thursday as scheduled for the annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>The economy minister was due to go to Frankfurt and London for a road show.</p>
<p>Telam said no reason was given by the economy ministry for the postponement of the trip.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
